<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1295 0 R
/E ( Factory pattern in PredictionMarketFactory: it allows markets to be deployed consistently and supports both normal CREATE deployment and deterministic CREATE2 deployment. This means future market addresses can be predicted before deployment, which is useful for frontend integration, indexing, and reproducible protocol behavior.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1296 0 R
/E ( UUPS upgradeability through PredictionMarketUpgradeable: implemented and tested a documented V1 to V2 upgrade path, including role-restricted upgrade authorization. This proves that the protocol can support future logic upgrades while protecting the upgrade process through access control.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1297 0 R
/E ( Checks-Effects-Interactions followed by the trading and liquidity functions use ReentrancyGuard where needed: this protects flows like buying shares, selling shares, adding liquidity, removing liquidity, and claiming rewards from common reentrancy risks. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1298 0 R
/E ( AccessControl roles protect the privileged operations: Minting, resolving markets, upgrading implementations, and depositing protocol fees are all role-gated. This avoids unguarded admin functions and makes the permission model clear for audit and governance.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1299 0 R
/E ( Oracle adapter pattern, Timelock governance, and a state-machine market lifecycle: oracle logic is separated from market logic, governance actions pass through a 2-day Timelock, and markets move through controlled states such as Open and Resolved. These patterns make the system more modular, auditable, and safer to extend.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
