<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 259 0 R
/T (Here we show the CI pipeline configured in GitHub Actions. The workflow runs on every push and pull request. It has three validation jobs. The first job checks Solidity formatting, builds contracts, runs the full Foundry test suite, generates gas and coverage reports, and performs Slither static analysis. The second job validates the subgraph by rebuilding contract artifacts, generating Graph types, and compiling the subgraph. The third job validates the frontend by installing dependencies, checking formatting, and producing a production build. In the final repository state, all three jobs passed successfully.)
/E (Here we show the CI pipeline configured in GitHub Actions. The workflow runs on every push and pull request. It has three validation jobs. The first job checks Solidity formatting, builds contracts, runs the full Foundry test suite, generates gas and coverage reports, and performs Slither static analysis. The second job validates the subgraph by rebuilding contract artifacts, generating Graph types, and compiling the subgraph. The third job validates the frontend by installing dependencies, checking formatting, and producing a production build. In the final repository state, all three jobs passed successfully.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
